{"kind":"promise","text":"Taking this. The measurements in the request are the starting point and I will not assume the characterisation of the root cause with them, as the request asks.\n\nOrder of work, because one condition gates the others. First reproduce the intermittent and capture the hidden stderr from a failing run, since the request states the diagnosis was in progress and not finished. What that stderr says decides whether the underlying defect is fixable here or has to be recorded as a known defect with its cause named — the request allows either, and I will not present a guess as a diagnosis.\n\nThen the separation itself: a case failure and a harness failure stop being the same word in what is printed and in the written evidence, and the captured stderr reaches the console on failure so a CI log alone carries the diagnosis. Then evidence survival past a failing CI run, choosing the retention window deliberately rather than taking a default, since these files describe adversarial cases.\n\nI will demonstrate both failure modes separately by forcing each, rather than inferring from one run, and check that a passing run is no noisier than today.\n\nOne thing I want to be honest about up front: if the intermittent turns out to be environmental — this machine runs several agents at once and I have been running full suites all session — then a fifty-percent rate measured here may not be the rate in CI, and I will say so rather than claim a fix for something I only made quieter."}